    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n48436" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θερμᾰσία</span></b> , ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>warmth, heat</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Aph.</u>
				5.63
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				860a19
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Epicur.
				<u>Ep.</u>
				2p.40U.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>HP</u>
				8.11.7
			</span></i>. <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Je.</u>
				28(51).39
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.S.
				3.34
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Paus.
				2.34.6
			</span></i>; <i>heating</i>, opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψῦξις</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>GA</u>
				764b7
			</span></i>: pl., <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.128f
			</span></i>. (The pure 
				Att.
			 words are <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θερμότης</span> and
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θέρμη</span>, Thom.Mag.<i><span class="en">
				p.179R.
			</span></i>, but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θερμασία</span> is used by
				<i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>An.</u>
				5.8.15
			</span></i>.)</div>
